    fix(dispatcher): decompose every repo spec and carry the section body into steps. Addresses DF-HELIX-7.
    
    `helix dispatch` failed on 15 of the repo's own 25 specs and, even when it
    succeeded, dispatched a single heading-shaped step with an empty
    expected_output because the spec body was never captured.
    
    Decomposition (pkg/dispatcher/decomposer.go) now follows an explicit fallback
    ladder instead of only recognising PHASE/FEATURE headings:
    
      1. the legacy rule, unchanged: H1 "# Helix Feature ..." and H2 headings
         containing PHASE or FEATURE still start tasks with the same IDs,
         priorities and order, so Phase/Feature specs decompose exactly as before;
      2. otherwise each H2 ("## 1. Mission", ...) section becomes one task;
      3. otherwise the whole file becomes ONE task titled from the H1, or from the
         filename when there is no H1.
    
    ErrDecomposeFailed is now reserved for empty or unreadable input; a readable
    document can no longer produce "no Phase or Feature sections found". Headings
    inside fenced code blocks are not boundaries, so markdown fences and shell
    comments ("# restart the container") cannot fracture a document.
    
    Body capture no longer dead code: Task gains an additive
    `Body string `json:"body,omitempty"`` holding the text between a task's heading
    and the next boundary. Description stays the heading text because callers
    depend on it, existing fields are untouched, and empty bodies are omitted from
    JSON.
    
    Steps are derived from that body: ForgejoLoop.Plan and AssignAgent now call the
    new DecomposeTaskWithBody, which extracts prose statements and list/table items
    from the section, joining wrapped lines into paragraphs before splitting on
    sentences and dropping markdown scaffolding (headings, table separator rows,
    fence content). Bodies that carry no prose - diagram-only sections - fall back
    to the description, and every step now gets a non-empty expected_output.
    DecomposeTask keeps its signature and legacy output (empty expected_output) for
    callers that pass only a description.
    
    Tests (pkg/dispatcher): a corpus test globs specs/*.md from the module root
    (found by walking up from the test file, failing loudly when the directory
    exists but is empty) and asserts no error, >= 1 task, non-empty Description
    and an ID for every task, unique IDs, and at least one non-empty Body per spec;
    focused regressions for the "# Title" + "## 1. Mission" shape, the
    "# Helix Feature 1 - X" single-task rule, PHASE heading preservation, the
    whole-file and filename-titled fallbacks, blank-input failure, fenced-heading
    safety, body-to-step extraction with the maxBodySteps cap, the unchanged
    DecomposeTask contract, and ForgejoLoop.Plan producing body-derived steps.
    Two pre-existing tests encoded the old never-decompose contract and were
    updated to it: their "no Phase/Feature" fixtures now assert the H2 split, and
    their error-path fixtures use a blank document, which is the only input that
    may still fail.
    
    Verified: gofmt clean, go vet ./... quiet, go build ./... exit 0,
    go test -short -count=1 ./pkg/dispatcher/... ./cmd/helix/... all ok, and
    `dispatch --dry-run` over all 25 specs/*.md exits 0 with no FAIL lines.
    
    Prompt: prompts/coding-hermes/v1.md
    
